-- title:
--   Affine blow-up chart C[I/a] under flat base change
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a commutative ring, $I \subseteq C$ an ideal and $a \in C$, and let $S$ be a $C$-algebra realising the localisation of $C$ away from $a$. Let $C'$ be a flat $C$-algebra, and let $S'$ be simultaneously a $C'$-algebra and a $C$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower $C \to C' \to S'$), realising the localisation of $C'$ away from the image of $a$ in $C'$; let $\varphi : S \to S'$ be any $C$-algebra homomorphism. Put $B := C[I/a]$, the $C$-subalgebra of $S$ generated by those $x \in S$ for which $x \cdot a = i$ in $S$ for some $i \in I$, and $B' := C'[IC'/a]$, the $C'$-subalgebra of $S'$ generated by those $x \in S'$ for which $x$ times the image of $a$ equals the image of some element of the ideal $I \cdot C'$ generated by the image of $I$. Let $\theta : C' \otimes_C B \to S'$ be the $C'$-algebra homomorphism determined by $c' \otimes b \mapsto c' \cdot \varphi(b)$. The assertion is that $\theta$ is injective and that its set-theoretic image consists exactly of the elements of $B'$; thus $\theta$ identifies $C' \otimes_C C[I/a]$ with $C'[IC'/a]$.
--
--   This is the affine-chart form of the statement that blowing up commutes with flat base change: the chart $C[I/a]$ of the blow-up of $I$, read inside $C[1/a]$, is compatible with a flat extension $C \to C'$. It is used to compare such an algebraised chart with the chart computed over a flat completion, in [`Subalgebra.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_adjoin_div_of_flat_of_dense`](thm.html#Subalgebra.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_adjoin_div_of_flat_of_dense).
